#import "/_lib/0.1.1.typ": *
#show: template

// #taxon[Taxon]
#title[X([n]) is an S_n-set]

Given a path $p: S=T$ in $B S_n$, any type family $X : B S_n -> "Set"$ gives a transport map
$
  "tr"_X (p) : X(S)->X(T).
$

In particular for $tau: [n] = [n]$ we have $"tr"_X (tau): X([n]) -> X([n])$.
So $X([n])$ becomes an $S_n$-set (see #local("00DI")[G-set]) with the action
$
  tau * x :-= "tr"_X (tau,x).
$
